I seem to get to dislike the UnNethack philosophy WRT wishing...
On dungeon level 2 I dipped to dilute a potion, got a djinn, got a wish.
I was allowed to wish for everything... - except for "magical items".
That's really great in a game full of magical items!
So I could NOT get dragon armor, rings of conflict, boots of speed, no
spellbook of magic missile, no gauntlets of power, amulet of reflection,
no marker, it seems generally no amulets, no rings, I didn't try wands.
The point is; once you're equipped enough to take the risk of dipping,
you rarely need any non-magical item any more.
Maybe it's possible to get magic item wishes deeper down in the dungeon
where the probabilities of fountain wishes are reduced?
Anyway, going to play a bit more until the character gets killed, then
back to Vanilla...

